00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:06.720
A useful feature within Word is
the ability to merge the contents

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.020
of a letter with a database of
clients' names and addresses.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.130
In this example, I'm going to use the
files that you can download from the

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:18.540
vision2learn website to show how you
can link the names and addresses of four

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.860
clients to the letter, which can then be
sent out without having to type out each

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.530
individual person's names and addresses.

00:00:27.389 --> 00:00:31.080
So the first thing I need to do is open
the letter which I have done on the

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.330
screen there and to access the mail merge
tool, I need to go to the mailings tab.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.190
So if I click on the mailings tab, this
brings up a range of options and the tool

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.629
we're going to use here is the mail merge.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:46.394
So if I click on the start mail merge,
select a step-by-step mail merge

00:00:46.394 --> 00:00:51.614
wizard, that will then bring up the
dialog box on the right-hand side.

00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:55.829
Now there are six steps in the
mail merge process and we'll work

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:56.999
through each one individually.

00:00:57.509 --> 00:01:00.139
So the first one is select document types.

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:01.889
So what type of document
are you working on?

00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:06.479
Well, we're working on a letter, so
we're happy with that and go to step

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:09.099
two and select the starting document.

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:10.859
So how do you want to set up your letters?

00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:14.849
And again, we're going to use the first
option here is use the current document.

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:18.239
You could go from a template
and start from an existing

00:01:18.239 --> 00:01:19.469
document that's somewhere else.

00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:23.084
So we'll now move to step three.

00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:25.394
Now, at this point, this is
where you're going to link the

00:01:25.394 --> 00:01:26.954
letter with the data source.

00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:32.324
So what you need to do is need to
browse to the location where you

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:35.684
saved the spreadsheet containing
the names and addresses, downloaded.

00:01:36.164 --> 00:01:40.994
So I saved these in my documents
folder in the IT course, and

00:01:40.994 --> 00:01:42.314
in the word processing folder.

00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:45.614
And you'll see this as an
Excel spreadsheet and it is

00:01:45.614 --> 00:01:47.234
sample mail merge addresses.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.344
So I just simply double click on that.

00:01:50.564 --> 00:01:52.274
And that then gives me the option.

00:01:52.604 --> 00:01:58.184
So it's asking me to select the table
and I'm happy with that click OK.

00:01:59.324 --> 00:02:01.994
This then brings up the mail
merge recipients dialog box.

00:02:02.264 --> 00:02:04.844
So this tells me what the
contents of the spreadsheet are.

00:02:05.174 --> 00:02:09.284
So I know there are four people
within that spreadsheet and the

00:02:09.284 --> 00:02:10.634
names and addresses are all there.

00:02:11.594 --> 00:02:16.109
If I didn't want to send the letter
to a specific person, I can tick or

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:17.939
untick that box and it will remove them.

00:02:17.939 --> 00:02:19.799
It won't include them in the merge.

00:02:21.279 --> 00:02:23.089
When I'm happy with that, I click OK.

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:27.299
And it is now time to
move on to the next step.

00:02:27.809 --> 00:02:32.669
So if I go to step four, this
is about write your letter.

00:02:32.669 --> 00:02:35.819
So if you hadn't already done so at
this point you would write the letter.

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:39.119
But what we need to do now is the
letter is already written, so we

00:02:39.119 --> 00:02:42.659
simply need to insert the address
block and the greeting line.

00:02:43.199 --> 00:02:46.994
So the address block is
traditionally inserted at the top

00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:48.254
left-hand section of the letter.

00:02:48.524 --> 00:02:52.394
So I will place the cursor there where
I want the address block to appear.

00:02:52.904 --> 00:02:57.764
And if I look along to the right if
I click on address block, I then have

00:02:57.764 --> 00:03:00.224
the insert address block dialog box.

00:03:00.974 --> 00:03:04.304
In here it will show me what
the addresses will look like.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.774
There are four recipients I know of,
so it will then preview each one.

00:03:09.044 --> 00:03:10.124
And I'm happy with that.

00:03:10.814 --> 00:03:13.504
So I can then select OK.

00:03:13.994 --> 00:03:16.754
So we'll insert the
address block merge field.

00:03:17.354 --> 00:03:20.884
I'm also going to add the greeting
line and the greeting line would be

00:03:20.884 --> 00:03:22.684
just above the main body of text.

00:03:22.684 --> 00:03:26.794
So I'll place the cursor there
and select greeting line.

00:03:27.824 --> 00:03:30.854
Again, this will give me a
dialogue box, which shows me a

00:03:30.884 --> 00:03:35.324
demonstration of a preview of
what will be seen on the letter.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:40.224
If I'm happy with that, I click OK
and that inserts the greeting line.

00:03:40.844 --> 00:03:44.209
So now what we need to do is
we need to preview the letters.

00:03:44.309 --> 00:03:46.799
So I click on step five.

00:03:47.969 --> 00:03:52.019
You can see that the address block and the
greeting line have changed and are now the

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:53.699
full names and addresses of the people.

00:03:54.779 --> 00:03:58.169
Again, I can preview each of the
letters to see that I'm happy with it.

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:05.479
I can exclude recipients, or I can even
edit the recipient list at this point.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.209
So the final step would
be to complete the merge.

00:04:08.195 --> 00:04:13.955
If I selected print, I can then select
all and I could print out the letters.

